# Relations this migration declares; probed by db-schema/tests/schema_fence.rs.
#
# Two ADD COLUMNs and an ADD CONSTRAINT against a table 0011 created, plus two
# `COMMENT ON COLUMN` statements. None of those is a relation, so the existence
# probe is blind to this migration's entire payload — the same position
# 0012_candle_price_checks is in, and the reasoning there applies unchanged: a
# CHECK that is dropped, weakened or merged applies cleanly and passes the whole
# fence while silently changing what the store accepts.
#
# So the behavior is asserted directly, by
# `fair_price_leg_stale_bounds_reject_what_they_name` in that same test file.
# Note what the existence probe would NOT catch even for the columns: they are
# NOT NULL, so a later migration making one nullable would keep the relation
# intact and quietly re-admit the unrecorded-bound rows this migration exists to
# forbid.
none alters a table 0011 created — adds columns, a CHECK and column comments, not a relation
